===Etymology===
{{confix|en|neuro|pathy}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} Any [[disease]] of the [[peripheral nervous system]]; peripheral neuropathy.<!--An instance of the idiomatic reality by which natural language uses some words that have obvious etymonic hypernymic potential as nonetheless usually meaning more specifically the principal hyponymic concept.-->
#: {{ux|en|Long-standing diabetes often causes '''neuropathy''' in the retinas, fingertips, and toes.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} Any [[disease]] of the [[nerve#Noun|nerves]] and [[nervous system]], usually and more specifically the peripheral nervous system, thus including both non-neuraxial and [[neuraxis#Noun|neuraxial]] instances of [[neural#Adjective|neural]] damage or dysfunction but excluding the neuraxis's [[psychiatry#Noun|psychiatric]] aspects ([[mental illness#Noun|mental illnesses]]).<!--An instance of the idiomatic reality by which natural language across speakers also nonetheless fails to invariably reserve those words exclusively to the hyponymic concept/sense.-->
#: {{ux|en|the contribution of central '''neuropathy''' on postural impairment observed in diabetic patients with peripheral '''neuropathy'''}}
#: {{ux|en|insights into the underlying molecular pathogenesis of diabetes-induced CNS '''neuropathy'''}}

